{"event_type":"review","id":"8b154a0c5a503f8c1cc7b23867b73f2b143164840e7f1443b40192388aa71b2d","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T16:09:00Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ab0b1ec74a7c6f7bd3050b2dd9745f7ddffbef6c5a3d923db4b9c6395a94187e","sha256":"ab0b1ec74a7c6f7bd3050b2dd9745f7ddffbef6c5a3d923db4b9c6395a94187e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d3a807ae210de63daac8d12d8c85501be0b5c7f59cfd14f9c4cf68c72e6bf4fc","sha256":"d3a807ae210de63daac8d12d8c85501be0b5c7f59cfd14f9c4cf68c72e6bf4fc"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2bfe7a0edda3d160d8731b2cbb6798eb2fcf3bac6def9cf8bfd400e5c6c489ae","sha256":"2bfe7a0edda3d160d8731b2cbb6798eb2fcf3bac6def9cf8bfd400e5c6c489ae"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b5d614b6a26f004183f48b21ddfa602e8f03db36246121b6f6125e835f8bbfb0","sha256":"b5d614b6a26f004183f48b21ddfa602e8f03db36246121b6f6125e835f8bbfb0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b2a583791876a946d694668d1854a7370f4d3285d6db83f9ce5bb78720047d40","sha256":"b2a583791876a946d694668d1854a7370f4d3285d6db83f9ce5bb78720047d40"}],"attempt_id":"4de4d526de513008ce6e8b365f833cfcc7b23171ddafef9b10fe65773952ca24:0:1","base":"c21df0488894ccf284b52cfd1771f2cc5d4d8ebc","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"5a2966b24aa0d017d49aa2f890f8e59b917b5aac","body":"**Reject an empty `--only` value.**\n\nIf a caller passes `--only \"\"`, `includes('')` matches every cell. The targeted rerun then becomes a full run. Reject the empty value before matching. `scripts/lib/eval-axes-select.mjs:17`\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  if (only === undefined || !cells.some((c) => `${c.lane}/${c.model}`.includes(only))) {\n+  if (only === undefined || only === '' || !cells.some((c) => `${c.lane}/${c.model}`.includes(only))) {\n```\n</details>","id":"a72b60bb9ffed10273ae8d8575ff9b471359768e82dd0fe23243f035a88051b9","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/lib/eval-axes-select.mjs","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject an empty `--only` value."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"b5fa5894dd5a9134ffa9b6bbfcda513f56542914","body":"**Filter credential keys that lack the listed name fragments.**\n\nIf the parent has `ENCRYPTION_KEY` or `SIGNING_KEY`, `scrubbedBuildEnv` passes that value to the build. Neither name matches `CREDENTIAL_NAME` or `CONNECTION_NAME`. Add these credential-name classes so the build does not inherit the keys.","id":"432d069ecbb3170363f27a43b4b2b7268db97e91face3609ef1b2fda35b1e110","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/lib/build-env.mjs","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Filter credential keys that lack the listed name fragments."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"b5fa5894dd5a9134ffa9b6bbfcda513f56542914","body":"**Filter credential-bearing URLs with username-only userinfo.**\n\nIf `DEPLOY_URL` contains `https://credential@example.invalid/`, the value passes through. `URL_WITH_PASSWORD` requires a colon before `@`, but URL userinfo can carry a credential without one. Filter credential-bearing userinfo in this form as well.","id":"188440a527b4e7485fb6a8410d03a65c1fc86f83c8efec2e341cdb9570f05206","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/lib/build-env.mjs","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Filter credential-bearing URLs with username-only userinfo."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"2f2d36a05f0e277a898238891df4e3d8ddac6b0d","body":"**`count('failures')` also matches `expected failures=`, so a passing Python run can fail the verdict.**\n\n`scripts/lib/test-narrow.mjs:241` builds `\\bfailures=(\\d+)`. The space before `failures` in `expected failures=N` is a word boundary, so this pattern also matches that text. unittest prints the info fields in the order `failures`, `errors`, `skipped`, `expected failures`, `unexpected successes`. If `failures=` is absent, `exec` returns the `expected failures` count instead.\n\nTwo concrete cases:\n- A clean run with an `@unittest.expectedFailure` test prints `OK (expected failures=1)`. The function then returns `failed=1` and `skipped=1`, and `passed` drops by 2. `pythonRunVerdict` at Line 261 sees `counts.failed > 0` and returns `result: 'fail'` for a run that exited 0.\n- `FAILED (errors=1, expected failures=2)` gives `failed = 2 + 1`, which counts the expected failures as failures.\n\nAnchor each key to the start of the list or to a `, ` separator.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  const count = (key) => Number(new RegExp(`\\\\b${key}=(\\\\d+)`).exec(last[3] ?? '')?.[1] ?? 0);\n+  const count = (key) =>\n+    Number(new RegExp(`(?:^|,\\\\s*)${key}=(\\\\d+)`).exec(last[3] ?? '')?.[1] ?? 0);\n```\n</details>\n\nAdd a regression case for `OK (expected failures=1)` and for `FAILED (errors=1, expected failures=2)` in `test/scripts/test-narrow.test.ts`.","id":"845c3d3e664f35b0362b73a881900ab8d9f61dbd7615928101aa820e20e39f0d","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/lib/test-narrow.mjs","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`count('failures')` also matches `expected failures=`, so a passing Python run can fail the verdict."}],"head":"a548c8104da47f2ca5dd8b6787771ab4250fd8dd","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"b5fa5894dd5a9134ffa9b6bbfcda513f56542914","intervals":[[1,30]],"path":"scripts/lib/build-env.mjs"},{"blob":"5a2966b24aa0d017d49aa2f890f8e59b917b5aac","intervals":[[1,40]],"path":"scripts/lib/eval-axes-select.mjs"},{"blob":"0dbb7574b2a9a48d6000758bcc6d2ca2e47b107f","intervals":[[1,110]],"path":"scripts/lib/github-settings.d.mts"},{"blob":"be2edaa074e705e6f905b8c3de493d08b256cf53","intervals":[[1,70]],"path":"scripts/lib/heavy-lock.d.mts"},{"blob":"47dd455f86a1cc05abdc33037